diff --git a/saas/README.md b/saas/README.md
index 28b0891..d598da4 100644
--- a/saas/README.md
+++ b/saas/README.md
@@ -105,3 +105,43 @@ knife ssh 'hostname:fizzy-lb-*' 'sudo docker exec fizzy-load-balancer kamal-prox
 ## License
 
 fizzy-saas is released under the [O'Saasy License](LICENSE.md).
+
+## Hosted billing
+
+Stripe hosts payment collection and subscription management. Configure these secrets
+(the price IDs must be recurring **monthly USD** prices):
+
+* `STRIPE_SECRET_KEY`
+* `STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET`
+* `STRIPE_MONTHLY_V1_PRICE_ID` — Unlimited, $20/month, unlimited cards, 5 GB
+* `STRIPE_MONTHLY_EXTRA_STORAGE_V1_PRICE_ID` — Unlimited+, $25/month, unlimited cards, 500 GB
+
+Free accounts include 1,000 published cards and 1 GB. Drafts do not consume the
+card allowance. Closed cards still count; deleted cards do not. The final 100
+cards show a countdown in the draft's publishing controls. At the limit, users
+can continue drafting and editing, but cannot publish or create cards via JSON.
+
+Enable Stripe's customer portal for payment methods, invoices, cancellation,
+and switching between the two approved prices. Subscribe the signed endpoint
+`POST /stripe/webhooks` (no account prefix) to `customer.subscription.created`,
+`customer.subscription.updated`, and `customer.subscription.deleted`. Checkout
+redirects never grant entitlements: signed subscription events do. Active and
+trialing subscriptions receive their plan; other statuses use Free. Scheduled
+cancellation keeps the paid allowance until the subscription ends. Unknown
+prices do not grant paid access.
+
+Account admins can upgrade or open the portal from settings. Staff can manage
+accounts at `/admin/accounts`. Comp grants the Unlimited allowance without a
+subscription, while preserving any existing paid plan. Uncomp removes that waiver;
+it does not change a Stripe subscription. Usage overrides replace measured card
+count and/or bytes used (blank uses measured usage, zero is valid). Reset deletes
+the override. Existing explicit storage exceptions continue to take precedence.
+
+Run the hosted tests offline with local Stripe stubs and signed webhook payloads:
+
+```sh
+SAAS=true DATABASE_ADAPTER=sqlite PARALLEL_WORKERS=1 bin/rails test saas/test
+```
+
+The billing migration runs on the `saas` database. Self-hosted installations do
+not load these routes, models, limits, or Stripe configuration.
diff --git a/saas/app/controllers/account/subscriptions/checkouts_controller.rb b/saas/app/controllers/account/subscriptions/checkouts_controller.rb
